# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
register_gate "tests/test_routes_pairing_bound.py" "ROUTES PAIRING BOUND GATE: PASS" "routes pairing bound" "cross-tier route pairing is BOUNDED (DoS fix): match_pairs was O(B×F×R×U) with no ceiling/no time budget (an N-route adversarial repo -> O(N⁴), measured 80 files = 55.7s, ~800 files ≈ 10h, starving the single event worker). Fix = invert to a concrete-segment index (probe only requests sharing a concrete anchor -> byte-identical couples since every match needs a shared concrete segment) + output cap _MAX_ROUTE_PAIRS + total-work budget _MAX_ROUTE_PAIR_PROBES. Proves: adversarial N stays bounded + caps hold + a token-collision repo that defeats the index is still bounded by the budget + a normal multi-framework repo yields the SAME couples as the pre-fix nested loop. Content-free, offline" "cross-tier route pairing DoS bound: the N⁴ nested loop is replaced by an inverted index + hard caps; adversarial repos are bounded in time while normal couples stay byte-identical (the existing route gates carry the rest of the semantics)" 10
